 ## Overview
-Intensity-to-Grayscale Mapping converts absolute scalar field intensity values into 8-bit grayscale luminance indices in the range $[0, 255]$ [S2, S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing high-precision floating-point data by compressing the dynamic range and enhancing contrast in low-intensity regions through gamma compression [S2, unofficial]. Unlike simple linear normalization, this method uses percentile-based saturation thresholds to ignore outliers and applies a non-linear power law to brighten subtle features [S2, unofficial].
