 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Division by Zero:** If the percentile threshold is $0$ or the global range is negligible, the denominator is clamped to $10^{-9}$ [S2, unofficial]. If the range is less than $10^{-6}$, return $0.0$ [S1, unofficial].
+- **Division by Zero:** If the global range is negligible ($i_{max} \approx i_{min}$), the denominator is clamped to $10^{-9}$ [S2, unofficial]. If the range is less than $10^{-6}$, return $0.0$ [S1, unofficial].
 - **NaN/Inf:** Non-finite values must be filtered or clamped before normalization to prevent propagation of NaNs [S2, unofficial].
 - **Clamping:** Normalized values must be clamped to $[0.0, 1.0]$ before applying gamma to ensure valid output [S2, unofficial].
